<p>Good question! A couple reasons:</p>
<p>1. A D-Class is almost definitely supervised by many people. The more people know about this SCP, the more people there are who are morally responsible for it, which is bad. An O5, though, is allowed to keep secrets.</p>
<p>2. An O5 is probably the most trustworthy person in the Foundation heirarchy for this sort of thing. A D-Class, or even a lower-level staff member, might be unreliable.</p>

