<p>Downvoted. It's one thing to create an SCP that is meant to raise an ethical dilemma. This is an SCP that essentially turns to the audience and says, &quot;Hello, I am an SCP that is meant to raise an ethical dilemma. Allow me to explain in detail the ethical dilemma I am raising, all the while pointing out that I am, once again, an ethical dilemma.&quot;</p>
<p>There are more interesting ways of raising a dilemma between deontological and consequentialist ethical stances than having the Foundation literally be attacked by deontological ethics while clip art of an actual trolley is displayed.</p>
<p>Also, what sort of tone were you going for with this article? Because making the threat too abstract and philosophical makes it not scary, and this is an SCP which goes a step further and makes the threat philosophy. It spells everything out, so there's no sense of mystery. It's not funny. It's not going for a tug at the heart strings. I don't know what I'm supposed to feel.</p>

							</div>

								
